{
  "info": {
    "name": "M16 â€” Reservations + Deposits + Seating",
    "description": "Nimbus POS M16: Reservations lifecycle, deposit tracking, and seating bridge.\n\n## Endpoints\n- POST /reservations â€” Create reservation\n- GET /reservations â€” List reservations (paginated, filterable)\n- GET /reservations/upcoming â€” List upcoming (PENDING/CONFIRMED)\n- GET /reservations/:id â€” Get reservation by ID\n- PATCH /reservations/:id/confirm â€” Confirm reservation\n- PATCH /reservations/:id/seat â€” Seat reservation (optional order creation)\n- PATCH /reservations/:id/cancel â€” Cancel reservation\n- PATCH /reservations/:id/no-show â€” Mark as no-show\n- POST /reservations/:id/deposits â€” Record deposit\n- GET /reservations/:id/deposits â€” List deposits\n- GET /reservations/:id/events â€” List events\n- PATCH /reservations/:id/assign-table â€” Assign table\n\n## Waiter MVP note (2026-05-18)\nAfter seed tightening, the Waiter role is denied on POST /reservations, PATCH /:id/confirm, PATCH /:id/cancel, POST /:id/deposits, and PATCH /:id/assign-table (403). Waiter retains pos:reservation:read and pos:reservation:seat only. PATCH /:id/seat now also flips the linked table to OCCUPIED. See WAITER-MVP-Role-Workflow.postman_collection.json folders E and H.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3001"
    },
    {
      "key": "accessToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "branchId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "reservationId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "tableId",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth â€” Login (Owner)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"owner@demo.local\",\n  \"password\": \"Owner#123\"\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "auth",
            "login"
          ]
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.environment.set('accessToken', body.accessToken);",
              "pm.test('Login OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Auth â€” Get /me (capture branchId)",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/me",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "me"
          ]
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "const bid = body.defaultBranch?.id || body.organizations?.[0]?.branches?.[0]?.id || body.memberships?.[0]?.branchId;",
              "pm.environment.set('branchId', bid);",
              "pm.test('Got branchId', () => pm.expect(bid).to.be.a('string'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Create Reservation",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "X-Branch-Id",
            "value": "{{branchId}}"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"customerName\": \"Postman Test Guest\",\n  \"partySize\": 4,\n  \"reservationAt\": \"{{$isoTimestamp}}\",\n  \"source\": \"PHONE\",\n  \"notes\": \"Test reservation via Postman\",\n  \"depositRequired\": 50000\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/reservations",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "reservations"
          ]
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.environment.set('reservationId', body.id);",
              "pm.test('Created 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
              "pm.test('Has reservation number', () => pm.expect(body.reservationNumber).to.match(/^RES-/));",
              "pm.test('Status PENDING', () => pm.expect(body.status).to.equal('PENDING'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "List Reservations",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "X-Branch-Id",
            "value": "{{branchId}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/reservations?page=1&pageSize=10",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "reservations"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "page",
              "value": "1"
            },
            {
              "key": "pageSize",
              "value": "10"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "pm.test('Has data array', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().data).to.be.an('array'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "List Upcoming Reservations",
